 3. 💰 Anthropic&#x27;s unavoidable IPO 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Jason Henry/Bloomberg via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Anthropic's impending IPO will test a jittery Wall Street, but investors say the timing isn't optional, Axios AI+ co-author Madison Mills writes. 

 The reason is simple math: The AI giant has grown too big for private fundraising. Why it matters: Top AI companies like Anthropic and OpenAI are racking up 12-figure spending commitments, straining the financial system's ability to keep up with a buildout that rivals America's railroads or interstate highways.

 Anthropic's computing commitments could reach $750 billion in the coming years, according to a draft IPO prospectus seen by The Wall Street Journal . 🔭 Zoom in: Investors say only public markets can raise money at that scale.

 OpenAI's most recent round, the biggest in history , took months to secure more than $120 billion — a feat unlikely to be repeated in this market. 🔮 What's next: Anthropic is expected to go public before Thanksgiving. A strong debut could help reset investor angst about the AI boom.

