 4. 🗳️ Where early voting is surging 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : UF Election Lab tracker. Map: David Adkins/Axios More than 12.6 million Americans have already cast ballots in the midterm elections, according to the University of Florida Election Lab's tracker .

 Georgia and Virginia lead reporting states in early turnout as a share of all ballots cast in the 2022 midterms, Axios' David Adkins and Herb Scribner write. Signs of strong early turnout are also emerging in other states.

 In Texas, Dallas County reported a record 76,079 in-person votes on Monday, the first day of early voting. In North Carolina, early voting was running 37% ahead of the same point in the 2022 midterms as of Oct. 18, with registered Democrats casting more than twice as many ballots as Republicans. Share this story . 

 
 
