 5. ✈️ Witkoff takes peace plan to Putin 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 White House envoy Steve Witkoff walks in Oslo yesterday before meeting Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Photo: Jonas Been Henriksen/NTB via Reuters White House envoy Steve Witkoff will meet Russian President Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg today and present him with an updated proposal to end the war in Ukraine, Axios' Barak Ravid reports. 

 President Trump's son-in-law and adviser Jared Kushner will join the meeting virtually. Why it matters: The White House hopes Putin will show more willingness to compromise after Trump agreed to lift sanctions on Russian diesel sales and took other steps welcomed by Moscow.

 Zelensky said yesterday that the next step should be a trilateral meeting between him, Putin and Trump — something Russia has refused to do so far.

